# GitLab Pages redirect rules, copied to the root of public/ by the
# `docs:publish` job. See .gitlab/ci/docs.yml.
#
# This host serves no content of its own. The main Quip documentation moved to
# developers.quip.network/docs under QUI-1272, and the XQuad book followed it to
# developers.quip.network/docs/xquad/ under QUI-1331, so every path here is a
# redirect. Domain-level (external) redirects are generally available since
# GitLab 17.4 and accept only 301/302.
#
# QUI-1272 landed the six documentation groups individually rather than as a
# catch-all, because a /* rule would have claimed /xquad/toolchain -- a path this
# host correctly 404'd while the book lived here, but which the docs host serves
# as a different document inside the book's own prefix. That objection is spent:
# the book is on the docs host now, /docs/xquad/toolchain redirects to
# /docs/xquad-toolchain there, and nothing is left here for a catch-all to shadow.
#
# public/404.html is deliberately gone with it. A /* rule makes it unreachable
# anyway, since ServeNotFoundHTTP runs only after both tryFile and tryRedirects
# miss, and a host with no content of its own has nothing to render a 404 for.
/  https://developers.quip.network/docs          301
/* https://developers.quip.network/docs/:splat   301
